actoryParameters[params] evidence; an observed init call alone is insufficient."}],"detail":"the reviewed source contains a call the specification itself names as governed; the event's own condition text is quoted so its limits are read with it"},"caller_contract":{"status":"callers_enumerated","files_with_calls":1,"call_sites":1,"same_file_call_sites":1,"receiver_resolved_call_sites":1,"searched_name":"tryToFindDefaultTrustManager","name_resolution":"direct","searched_declaring_file":true,"callers":[{"source_file_path":"data/src/main/java/org/cryptomator/data/cloud/webdav/network/DefaultTrustManager.kt","call_sites":[{"line":43,"receiver":"","resolution":"declaring_file","qualified_type":"","arity":0}],"declaring_file":true}],"detail":"every file in the checkout that calls `tryToFindDefaultTrustManager` is listed","catalog_callers_of_target":1},"input_flow":{"status":"no_editable_text_parse","parse_calls":[],"unguarded_in_framework_callback":0,"bound":"Read from the reviewed method's text. An editable text widget can always yield an empty string, and a numeric inputType prevents neither that nor a value beyond the parser's range, so invalid input is feasible for a parse call fed straight from one. enclosed_by_try_that_catches is lexical: no try in this method catches a parse failure at that call. in_framework_callback means the call sits in a listener or on* callback the framework invokes, so no caller in the repository can handle its exception. validation_search, when present, is what a search of the repository's Java/Kotlin sources and layouts found for these widgets: validation calls that name them (watchers, filters, setError), an emptiness check in the method, the layout attributes of their view ids, the helpers they are passed to, and any global exception handler. no_validation_found_for_any_widget means none exists in the repository, so an empty field reaches the parse; widget_passed_to_helpers_that_may_validate and validation_found_for say what remains open