categories, and optional extraction of TrustManager objects. The representative message, "expecting one of PKIX,SunX509 but found .", corresponds to the algorithm-membership constraint, not to a certificate-chain-validation result.","detector_semantics":{"claim":"For the representative finding, the detector claims that the algorithm value associated with a TrustManagerFactory.getInstance call did not satisfy the reported CrySL allowlist requiring PKIX or SunX509.","predicates":["algorithm in {"PKIX", "SunX509"}","Get precedes Init on the tracked TrustManagerFactory object.","Init(KeyStore) requires generatedKeyStore[keyStore] evidence.","Init(ManagerFactoryParameters) requires generatedManagerFactoryParameters[params] evidence.","Init is described as ensuring generatedTrustManager[this].","Optional GetTrustMng is described as ensuring generatedTrustManagers[trustManager]."],"limitations":["The supplied rule description does not define the detector's interprocedural, alias, reflection, Kotlin-desugaring, or unknown-value treatment.","The supplied rule description does not explain why the report renders the found value as ".".","The two-value allowlist does not establish portability across all JSSE or Android providers.","The optional getTrustManagers event does not express later SSLContext configuration or an actual TLS handshake.","The exact CrySL rule revision and compiled artifact used by the detector are not verified."]},"api_semantics":{"documented_behavior":["javax.net.ssl.TrustManagerFactory is a provider-based factory for TrustManager objects.","Its getInstance overloads request a trust-management algorithm.","init(KeyStore) initializes the factory from certificate authorities and related trust material; init(ManagerFactoryParameters) accepts provider-specific trust material.","getTrustManagers returns the resulting managers; supplied Android reference context states it throws IllegalStateException if the factory was not initialized.","Supplied Java standard-